F2  The "H1a fix" in the parallel lane was itself a new infinite loop.
    process_one_task() returned status "skipped_breaker" for attempts>=3, but
    the results loop only knew two branches: failed (res None) or done. A
    breaker-skipped task was marked "failed" — and "failed" tasks are re-selected
    as pending every cycle. Result: the same task was re-dispatched, instantly
    re-skipped, and re-failed in a ~2-second tight loop FOREVER, with no log
    line explaining it. The audit-5 "bounded loop" fix created an unbounded one.
F3  Double attempt-counting in the parallel lane: attempts was incremented
    pre-call inside process_one_task AND again on success in the results loop,
    so a first-time parallel task ended with attempts=2 — corrupting every
    downstream "< 3" retry guard.
